61
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Then use the linear virtual model tool to draw the area along the forehead model.

62
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Start drawing from the front of the nose here.

63
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Click to create a straight line point.

64
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Press Ctrl and click to draw a straight line point.

65
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
You can freely draw these lines on the model.

66
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
These lines will become the contact points between the line and the line.

67
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
This step is a bit like a retouch.

68
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Draw a large division, and then draw these versions according to the need.

69
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:46,000
When drawing to extract the area, be careful to avoid the position near the eyeball.

70
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
And ensure that the shape is closed.

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:56,000
If you want to adjust these points, you can use the linear virtual model tool to drag them.

72
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,000
When the structure is completed, we will extract the version from the model.

73
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Use the flat flat version tool to select all areas to extract the version.

74
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Then press the Enter key to extract the version.

75
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Place the extracted version in the 2D window.

76
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Select the version on this side.

77
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Press Ctrl to align the version.

78
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Then sew the balance line in the middle.

79
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Then apply the full grain leather fabric to these versions.

80
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Open the simulation.

81
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
You will see that the entire head version has no wrinkles.

82
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
The seam allowance is also relatively smooth.

83
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Then adjust the section of the version.

84
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Try to keep the corner of the bottom of the front as straight as possible.

85
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
This way, the left and right sides are balanced together, which is a flat corner.

86
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
